  "id": "Compound::DB01078 - Gene::478",
  "verbalization": "Deslanoside appears to interact with Atp1a3 through a series of mechanistic pathways that involve the regulation of sodium-potassium ATPase activity. The evidence suggests that Deslanoside binds to Fxyd2, which is involved in potassium transport, and this interaction leads to the participation of Fxyd2 in potassium-transporting ATPase activity, ultimately resulting in the participation of Atp1a3. Similarly, Deslanoside also binds to Atp1b2, which is a related isoform of the sodium-potassium ATPase, and this interaction contributes to the participation of Atp1a3 in the same activity. The final score for both paths indicates a strong, consistent relationship between Deslanoside and Atp1a3, suggesting a potential role for Deslanoside in modulating the activity of the sodium-potassium ATPase, which is critical for maintaining cellular homeostasis. The integration of these pathways highlights a plausible mechanism by which Deslanoside may influence Atp1a3 function, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the clinical relevance of this interaction.",
